# Boolean fit gates (scripts/gate.sh): "<part> empty" must render zero
# facets, "<part> interferes" is the mandatory negative control.
#
# fitcheck      — every pairwise intersection across the three printed
#                 bodies (body / screw / moving jaw) at the pose extremes
#                 0.5 mm off closed and full open. The motion is a monotone
#                 translation and every clearance in play (rails 0.3, floor
#                 0.6, saddle straddle 0.3, thread fit by construction) is
#                 pose-independent, so the extremes bound the whole travel.
#                 Must be empty.
# fitcheck_neg  — the same jaw grown 0.4 mm every way it slides; must
#                 interfere, proving the empty check can fail.
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
